This file says which licence applies to what. The full licence texts are in LICENSES/ (also at https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar/tree/main/LICENSES). REUSE.toml states the same rules file by file, in the machine-readable REUSE format (https://reuse.software).


WHICH LICENCE APPLIES

Paths are relative to the library's root folder (in the plugin directory edition: skills/lemo-opuscar/library/). The first rule that matches a file decides.

1. Third-party material keeps its own licence: fonts and their licence texts, music, sound recordings and sample libraries, models and textures, data, maps, footage, photographs, and the code libraries bundled with some demos. Each demo's CREDITS names its third-party assets and their licences; REUSE.toml names every third-party file kept in this repository and its licence.

2. Docs: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0, LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt).
   - Every Markdown file (*.md): the guides, each style's STYLE.md and DEMO.md, the READMEs, and the Markdown of the Claude Code skill.
   - The image-generation prompts: everything under styles/*/demo/prompts/, styles/manga-panels/demo/tools/style_suffix.txt and styles/comic-history/demo/tools/sheets.json.

3. Demo films, and pictures made from them: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0, LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt).
   - The demo films and the other films of this project, published in the repository's Releases and on its gallery site, and their subtitles (styles/*/*.srt).
   - Their posters and stills (styles/*/poster.jpg, styles/*/demo/stills/).
   - The pictures under docs/ and styleboard/img/, made from the films for the README and the gallery site.
   Third-party material in the films and in these pictures (footage, photographs, satellite imagery, music, maps and model data) keeps its own licence: each demo film's CREDITS (styles/<slug>/demo/CREDITS) names it, and REUSE.toml names it for the posters, stills and cards made from such material.

4. Code: MIT License (LICENSES/MIT.txt). Everything else that is ours: the code in core/, tools/, styleboard/ and plugin/ and each demo's code, with the data, configuration, CREDITS and small assets they use. Where the MIT text speaks of "this software and associated documentation files (the "Software")", it means the material under this rule only, not the docs of rule 2.

Two styles were contributed from outside: Memphis Diorama by EianLu (styles/memphis-diorama/) and Crayon World 3D by 2nd1st (styles/crayon-world/). They are included under these terms with their authors' permission, which also covers the commercial licence below: Lemomo (LemoLab) gives it for their docs as for the rest.

Six voice tracks are excluded from rule 3 and from any licence here: the narration in the demo films of Chalkboard, Circuit Board, Tabletop App Flythrough, Isometric People Scene and Scratchboard Long Take (made with Microsoft Edge TTS, an online service) and of Broadcast News Package (made with Doubao TTS, under Volcengine's terms). Don't extract them or reuse them in other work. Each of these six films may still be shared whole, as published, under CC BY 4.0 for everything but its narration.

Clawd is excluded from rules 3 and 4 and from any licence here. Clawd, the small orange character, is Anthropic's: its design and its name belong to Anthropic. It appears, for example, in OPUSCAR 98, in the thank-you films for 300, 800, 3,000 and 6,000 stars and in the demo film of Mascot Screencast, in pictures made from them, and in the Mascot Screencast code that draws it; this paragraph applies as well to any other film, picture or code of this project in which it appears. REUSE.toml marks such files kept in this repository with LicenseRef-Clawd. No licence is given here for Clawd, and none for any trademark. These films and pictures may still be shared whole, as published, under CC BY 4.0, and the code used under MIT, for everything but Clawd.

Third-party product interfaces, names, logos and trademarks that appear in the films, pictures and code (for example Anthropic's Claude app interface and the names Claude and Claude Code in Mascot Screencast) belong to their owners and are not licensed here. This applies as well where only a name appears (for example GPT, Claude and Gemini in Rhythm Game Show, or Google and Meta in Broadcast News Package). REUSE.toml marks, with LicenseRef-ThirdPartyMarks, the pictures and code that redraw such an interface or logo. The films and pictures may still be shared whole, as published, under CC BY 4.0, and the code used under MIT, for everything but those.


FILMS YOU MAKE

Films you make with the library are yours, commercial films included, and need no credit; third-party material you use in them (for example samples under CC BY) keeps its own terms.


ADDITIONAL PERMISSION FOR THE DOCS

In addition to CC BY-NC 4.0, Lemomo (LemoLab) grants a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, irrevocable permission to you and the people working with you on a film (staff, contractors, the client) to read, follow, copy and adapt the docs to make your own films (commercial and client films included), and to include them, or versions you adapted, in the project files you deliver for that film. A style you change and keep as your own to make your films (MY-STYLES.md) is covered. This permission does not cover sharing the docs or adapted versions with others beyond those people and those project files, or selling them: CC BY-NC 4.0 and the commercial licence below govern those.


HOW TO CREDIT

"Lemo-Opuscar by Lemomo (LemoLab)", with a link to https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, the name of the licence with a link to it (CC BY-NC 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/, for the docs; CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/, for the films and pictures), and say if you changed it.

For the two contributed styles, name their author too: "Memphis Diorama by EianLu, in Lemo-Opuscar by Lemomo (LemoLab)" and "Crayon World 3D by 2nd1st, in Lemo-Opuscar by Lemomo (LemoLab)".

Third-party material is credited as its CREDITS says.


COMMERCIAL USE OF THE DOCS

Any commercial use of the docs beyond the permission above (for example selling them, or putting them, whole, in part or adapted, into a product or service run for commercial advantage, paid or not) needs a commercial licence. To ask for one, email lemomo.studio@gmail.com.


EARLIER VERSIONS

Versions of this repository published before 2.0.0, and forks made from them, keep the licence they were published under.
